    question:'People arriving from Africa, Madagascar, India, China and Europe spoke many different languages, yet had to work, trade and live side by side every day.<br>What does that best explain?',
    options:['Why a shared everyday language grew up and is spoken across communities','Why each community kept its own language completely separate from all others','Why only one language from overseas survived and all the rest disappeared','Why written records were kept in a language that nobody actually spoke'],
